Z||000000||Fierochic88||07-19-2001||08:04 PM||||Awhile back this came up while we were discussing the Atari.  Anyone else remember these early PC's?  I've had one ever since I was about 5 but haven't fired it up in years.  My dad runs his huge model train layout partially off of them too, he has them running at the speed of older IBM's.  Crazy stuff.<P>So what was everyone's favorite game?  Personally mine were many but I really like Goonies, Spelunker, Frogger and Smurfs.  Hot Wheels was also pretty slick!<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||07-19-2001||08:12 PM||||I remember the commodore I had in 1st grade  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||07-19-2001||08:16 PM||||Commodore 64 had ScreamTracker, That program ROCKED....  The first home audio mixing program....    Anyone else remember .MOD and .S3M ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||07-19-2001||08:57 PM||||My friend had a Commodore 64.  I remember only two games... one of them was ghostbusters which we could never beat.  I also had the Atari 2600 version of the game.  The other was Blueprint.  It was a cartridge game that plugeged into the back of the computer!  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||07-19-2001||09:10 PM||||I used to play a golf game on a 64. Doens't quite compare to playing Links LS online anymore  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I actually have a Commodore Amiga sitting in a cupboard gathering dust. God knows why. Maybe I want to start an antique computer museum someday.<P>On the scarey side there is a club in my town for Commodore 64 owners, they think the things are the ants pants of computers. Wonder if any of them have actually used a real computer yet.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000005||DecadenceR||07-19-2001||09:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>I remember the commodore I had in 1st grade   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was in a poor school in 1st grade, but I remember computer class in second grade that we had a picture contest on drawing with BASIC commands... And the triangle they called the turtle.. LOL||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||07-19-2001||11:39 PM||||I always wanted a commodore 64 when i was a kid, and i have played a friends 128 a long time ago.<P>Last year, i bought one on ebay with a color monitor.  Shipping was costly but it was fun to play with for a week.  My rooms a mess, so i put it back in the box.  I did buy tons of games of ebay, plus a plug in, to increase the speed for processing software.||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||07-19-2001||11:46 PM||||My favorite C64 game was Technocop followed by Skyfox. Anyone remember the Epyx Olympic games? I adore my 64!!!!!<P>Aus, what kind of Amiga do you have kicking around?||||reg||10
Z||000008||AkursedX||07-19-2001||11:51 PM||||I liked the Gi Joe game that they had for the Commordore64.  It was like the original streetfighter! I used to play that all the time at one of my friends house's.  That game resulted in alot of missed homework, lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||kslish||07-19-2001||11:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loafer87gt:<BR><B>Anyone remember the Epyx Olympic games?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I remember playing one called Track & Field.  I didn't have a C64 for long (borrowed a relatives) since I had an Apple II back then.  I also remember that the keyboard sorta sucked on the C64.  That's about it.<P>As for elementary school, we had Tandy TRS-80 Model 4's.  Monochrome display and an awesome 16K of memory.  We had one game (Lunar Lander) and we did that screen drawing stuff too with the "turtle" cursor.  I believe the language used to control the turtle was called LOGO or something and not BASIC, but could be wrong.  <P>Ahhh, computing in the early 80's.....<P>Ken S.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Steve Normington||07-20-2001||01:47 AM||||Anyone use the tape drive as your secondary storage device? "Push play and wait 5 hours."||||reg||1
Z||000011||AusFiero||07-20-2001||01:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loafer87gt:<BR><B>Aus, what kind of Amiga do you have kicking around?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow I dug it out for a look. I have a lot more than just an old amiga  Amiga. It is complete Commodore Amiga 520 model. Found I even have the monitor, a printer, an extra external floppy drive, a modem, and some accessories I can't even remember what they are for. I hooked it all up. Guess what. It works perfectly. Wonders never cease. Now combine that with the old XT in the garage and the 386 hidden somewhere in the house I think I almost got a museum. <P>Maybe I should go through my cupboard in my study and see what else I got. I got a few big boxes of all sorts of bits. Memory, video cards, modems...god just all sorts of bits everywhere. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
