Z||000022||Fformula88||07-20-2001||05:30 PM||||We never could get all the men under the Stay Puffed Marshmallow man.  I have beaten the game on the Atari, but never on the C64.<P>I owned an Amiga 500 for years!  Its too bad it never became more popular because it was a great system.  The operating system was a lot like a Macintosh, but far better at the time.  The games were also way better than their equivalent IBM/PC counterparts.  I will never remember all the games, but Gunship, Silent Service, TV Sports Football and Earl Weaver baseball all come to mind as good games!  To this day there isn't a baseball game that is as good statistically or strategy wise as EWB IMO!||||reg||1
