Z||000027||Tonker||07-21-2001||11:52 PM||||My Favourite game for my C64 was Racing Destruction. It was awesome!! You could play head to head, change gravity settings drop oil slicks, there were jumps and tunnels. It was as good as some pc games that came out a decade later.<P>Oh yeah and the hacked strip poker game I got from a friend wasn't bad either...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000028||grinthock||07-22-2001||09:10 AM||||Let's see, what have I had.....<P>Started on a TRS-80 Model 1, top of the line, had the 10 MEG Hard Drive (about the size of a home stereo receiver!) and the printer, expansion unit (took it to 128K!)<P>Then got the Tandy CO-CO Colour Computer, had the tape, but picked up a double disk drive (great for pireacy)<P>Got my Tandy 1000 - 8088, 640K Ram (upgraded) it was enough to play LSL (that was a great game, anybody know what LSL is?) had a 40MEg HArd drive card in it...  The hard drive motor wore after a couple years and if the machien stopped I had to open the case and spin the pintle with needle nose pliers to get it going cause the brushes were going on it.<P>And then had the 1000TX 80286, then a 1000TL2 which was another 80286 with Tandy 3-voice sound, and I even got a SoundBlaster for christmas that year cost over $300 !  DAMN expensive<P>When I was 8 I started my own BBS, connected to the FidoNet Network, I was on it for YEARS, infact if you checkout the world wide BBS list (i forget the url) I am listed (The Dynamic BBS, Acidic Reality, The Unholy Realms, and all hte other names it ran under)<P>Then got a 386, then my 486-dx2 66, then a P120, then a P133, then a P200, then a PII 266, then a Celery 400, only to rest at my current toy.... P4-1.7Ghz, 512RDRAM and geez I could spend all day inventorying the stuff I STILL have and the stuff that runs, I am a big tower nut so all my towers are 3 feet tall and have LOTSA stuff in it...||||reg||1
